.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt CUDA-NATIVE-TOOLCHAIN 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cuda-native-toolchain
.Nd compile and link CUDA source with the non-executing cuda-native SDK
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm sh
.Pa lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh
.Ar outdir
.Pp
.Nm sh
.Pa lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh
.Fl -check-llvm
.Pp
.Nm clang++
.Fl x Cm cuda
.Fl -cuda-path Ns = Ns Ar outdir
.Fl -cuda-gpu-arch Ns = Ns Ar arch
.Fl -cuda-device-only
.Fl S
.Ar file.cu
.Pp
.Nm clang++
.Fl x Cm cuda
.Fl -cuda-path Ns = Ns Ar outdir
.Fl -cuda-gpu-arch Ns = Ns Ar arch
.Ar file.cu
.Fl L Ns Ar outdir/lib64
.Fl l Ns Cm cudart
.Fl Wl,-rpath, Ns Qq $PWD/ Ns Ar outdir/lib64
.Sh DESCRIPTION
cuda-native is a CUDA stack for
.Fx
that uses no NVIDIA proprietary file.
This page describes its first piece: the SDK tree that clang takes as a CUDA
installation.
The tree holds headers written from the public CUDA API references and from
what clang's own CUDA runtime wrapper includes by name.
It does not hold a single file of NVIDIA's CUDA toolkit.
.Pp
.Pa mksdk.sh
assembles the tree in
.Ar outdir ,
which must be new or empty:
.Bl -tag -width "nvvm/libdevice/libdevice.10.bc"
.It Pa include/
the SDK headers;
.Pa cuda.h
sets
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
to 13000, and clang takes the SDK version from it.
.It Pa bin/
the executable
.Nm nvptxas
and
.Nm nvfatbin
programs, also installed as
.Nm ptxas
and
.Nm fatbinary
for clang, and
.Nm cuda-objdump ,
which lists the members of a fatbin container.
.It Pa lib64/
the non-executing
.Pa libcudart.so.13
and its relative
.Pa libcudart.so
linker symlink.
.It Pa share/cuda-native/schema/
the JSON schemas for tool versions, optional tool traces and runtime events.
.It Pa nvvm/libdevice/libdevice.10.bc
the device library that clang links into every device compile.
.It Pa version.json
cuda-native's own name and version, generated from the
.Dv CUDA_VERSION
and
.Dv CUDA_NATIVE_VERSION
macros of
.Pa cuda.h .
clang does not read it.
.El
.Pp
With
.Fl -check-llvm ,
.Pa mksdk.sh
runs the same LLVM tool and clang version checks as a build, prints
.Ql llvm: <prefix> clang <major> ,
and creates nothing.
It exits 0 when the LLVM install is usable and 2 otherwise, with the same
refusal diagnostic as a build.
.Pp
The compiler is clang from LLVM 23
.Pq the ports Pa llvm23 No package .
The base system clang is not used.
The tested
.Ar arch
values are
.Cm sm_120
.Pq compute capability 12.0, GeForce RTX 50 series such as the GB206 ,
.Cm sm_121
.Pq compute capability 12.1, DGX Spark GB10 ,
and their architecture-specific forms
.Cm sm_120a
and
.Cm sm_121a .
The output is PTX ISA 9.x text.
Other arch values that clang knows, such as
.Cm sm_120f
and
.Cm sm_121f ,
are not refused, but they are not tested.
.Pp
With
.Fl -cuda-host-only Fl c
clang builds the host object.
It leaves the launch calls
.Pq Fn cudaLaunchKernel , Fn __cudaPushCallConfiguration , Fn __cudaPopCallConfiguration
for the runtime library to provide.
Without a host-only or device-only option, clang runs both tool stubs and can
link the host program against the stub runtime.
The cubin-placeholder header preserves PTX after its separator, and the
diagnostic fatbin container records member sizes and hashes; neither contains
executable GPU machine code.
Every launch returns
.Dv cudaErrorNotSupported
.Pq 801 .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width LLVM
.It Ev LLVM
The LLVM install that
.Pa mksdk.sh
and the test use; its clang must be version 23 or later.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/llvm23 .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Where the test makes its scratch directory; the default is
.Pa /tmp .
.It Ev CUDA_NATIVE_TRACE
When nonempty, the installed tool stubs append JSONL call records to this file.
The records can be validated with the schemas installed under
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/ .
.It Ev CUDA_NATIVE_STUB_TRACE
When set exactly to
.Ql 1 ,
the runtime stub writes JSON registration and launch events that conform to
.Pa share/cuda-native/schema/cuda-native-stub-trace-1.schema.json
to standard error.
Any other nonempty value names a file to which the JSON lines are appended.
An unset or empty value disables that trace.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "tests/cuda_native_toolchain_test.sh" -compact
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/sdk/
the sources of the tree
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/libdevice/libdevice.ll
the device library source
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/tools/
the POSIX shell sources of both device-tool stubs
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/libcudart-stub/cudart_stub.c
the launch and registration runtime source
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/schema/
the versioned tool-version, tool-trace and runtime-trace JSON schemas
.It Pa lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh
the assembler of the tree
.It Pa tests/cuda_native_toolchain_test.sh
the test: the tree, PTX for all four arches, full compiles, traces, link and run,
registration IR, provenance and mutants
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Pa mksdk.sh
exits 0 when the tree is built, 2 when the arguments or
.Ar outdir
are refused, the LLVM tools are missing or older than 23, and 1 when a step fails.
A failed run leaves no partial tree:
.Ar outdir
stays absent or empty, because the tree is built next to it and renamed
into place at the end.
If
.Ar outdir
changes while the tree is built, the run fails and says so.
.Pp
With
.Fl -check-llvm ,
.Pa mksdk.sh
exits 0 when the LLVM install is usable and 2 otherwise, including a usage error.
.Pp
The test exits with the number of failed checks, capped at 76 so that it is
never confused with 77.
It exits 77 when no clang 23 or later is found in
.Pa $LLVM/bin
and every check that ran passed (the checks that need LLVM are skipped),
and 99 when it cannot set up.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Build the tree and emit PTX for the GB10:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sh lib/cuda-native/mksdk.sh obj/cuda-native
/usr/local/llvm23/bin/clang++ -x cuda --cuda-path=obj/cuda-native \e
    --cuda-gpu-arch=sm_121 --cuda-device-only -S -o vadd.ptx vadd.cu
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr clang 1 ,
.Xr cuda-objdump 1 ,
.Xr nvfatbin 1 ,
.Xr nvptxas 1 ,
.Xr libcudart-stub 3 ,
.Xr nvfatbin 5
.Sh HISTORY
The SDK tree first appeared in the native CUDA work on Track #2380, stage C1.1
.Pq Track #2425 .
.Sh CAVEATS
The following pieces are missing:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
The device library has no functions yet.
A kernel that calls a math function such as
.Fn sinf
leaves an unresolved
.Li __nv_*
symbol in its PTX.
A later release adds a device library built from libclc.
.It
The
.Nm ptxas
and
.Nm fatbinary
programs are deliberately non-assembling stubs.
The former writes a
.Li CUDA-NATIVE-STUB-CUBIN 1
placeholder with unchanged PTX after its header; the latter records all
supplied payloads in the
.Li CUDA-NATIVE-STUB-FATBIN 1
diagnostic container.
Neither produces executable GPU machine code.
.It
The stub
.Nm libcudart
implements only clang's launch bookkeeping and validated host-side registration.
Every launch returns 801 and no device code runs.
There is no general CUDA runtime implementation and no
.Nm libcuda
yet.
.El
.Pp
The headers declare only what clang's wrapper and the test kernels need.
.Fn atomicAdd
lowers to a system-scope atomic.
That is stronger than the device scope CUDA defines, so the results are
correct but it may be slower; a later release changes it.
